  "notes": "A formal, literary word for losing consciousness and falling down. More dramatic and serious in tone than casual expressions for fainting. Often used in news reports and written narratives.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {昏倒|こんとう}する: to faint, to collapse unconscious\n- その{場|ば}で{昏倒|こんとう}する: to collapse on the spot\n- {昏倒|こんとう}{状態|じょうたい}: state of unconsciousness\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {気絶|きぜつ}: fainting — more general and common term for losing consciousness\n- {卒倒|そっとう}: fainting — similar meaning, slightly more literary\n- {失神|しっしん}: loss of consciousness — medical term focusing on the neurological state\n- {倒|たお}れる: to collapse/fall down — broader term, does not necessarily imply unconsciousness",
